id: bootloader_em4_gpio_retention
label: EM4 GPIO Retention
package: bootloader
description: >
  The Bootloader EM4 GPIO Retention component provides functionality to retain and restore GPIO states
  specifically during OTA upgrades using EM4 sleep and wakeup cycles. It supports preserving GPIO configurations,
  output states, and reset information during EM4 transitions for bootloader operations. The component uses BURAM
  (Backup RAM) for storage and provides APIs for pin configuration, reset counter management, and
  automatic GPIO restoration on wakeup. Features include BURAM-based reset reason tracking, configurable pin retention
  (up to 16 pins), and seamless integration with existing bootloader reset mechanisms.
category: Platform|Bootloader|Core
quality: production
source:
- path: platform/bootloader/em4-gpio-retention/btl_em4_gpio_retention.c
  condition: [device_series_2]
include:
- path: platform/bootloader/em4-gpio-retention
  file_list:
  - path: btl_em4_gpio_retention.h
define:
- name: BTL_EM4_GPIO_RETENTION
  value: 1
provides:
- name: bootloader_em4_gpio_retention
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: MSLA
root_path: bootloader
